  "last_message": "I've implemented `can_cancel`, and all 6 tests pass (the 2 existing ones plus 4 new ones).\n\nThe rule comes from `docs/features/cancellation.md`: a member can cancel a pantry order until 2 hours before its pickup slot starts, and not after. That's when the volunteers pack the bags.\n\n- **`larder/cancellation.py`**: `can_cancel` returns `now <= pickup_starts - timedelta(hours=CUTOFF_HOURS)`, with `CUTOFF_HOURS = 2`. I followed the same constant-plus-`timedelta` style as `larder/sessions.py`.\n- **`tests/test_cancellation.py`**: new tests for one minute before the cutoff (allowed), exactly at the cutoff (allowed), one minute after (refused) and once pickup has started (refused).\n\n**Decision for you:** the docs don't say what happens at exactly 2 hours before pickup. I read \"until 2 hours before\" as including that moment, so a cancellation then is allowed. If packing starts right at the 2-hour mark, change `<=` to `<` and flip the at-cutoff test. It would be worth adding the answer to the Cutoff section of the doc.",
